#, fuzzy
msgid "MicroProfile Fault Tolerance support"
msgstr "Soporte de tolerancia a fallos de microperfiles"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Quarkus Tools for Visual Studio Code 1.4.0 has been released on the\n"
"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=redhat.vscode-quarkus[VS Code Marketplace]."
msgstr "Quarkus Tools para Visual Studio Code 1.4.0 ha sido publicado en el link:https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=redhat.vscode-quarkus[Mercado de VS Code] ."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/[vscode-quarkus] 1.4.0 fixes several bugs, including some performance issues, but the highlights of this release revolve around bringing support for multiple MicroProfile modules (Fault Tolerance, Health, LRA, Metrics, Open API, Open Tracing, Rest Client), in both properties and Java files.\n"
"Many of these MicroProfile related enhancements were contributed by IBM."
msgstr "link:https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/[vscode-quarkus] 1.4.0 corrige varios errores, incluidos algunos problemas de rendimiento, pero lo más destacado de esta versión gira en torno a la incorporación de soporte para múltiples módulos MicroProfile (Tolerancia de fallos, Salud, LRA, Métricas, API abierta, Rastreo abierto, Cliente Rest), tanto en las propiedades como en los archivos Java. Muchas de estas mejoras relacionadas con MicroProfile fueron aportadas por IBM."

#, fuzzy
msgid "For a list of all changes, please refer to the https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md[changelog]."
msgstr "Para ver una lista de todos los cambios, consulte el  link:https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md[registro de cambios]."

#, fuzzy
msgid "Watch a demo video of all features presented in this article:"
msgstr "Vea un vídeo de demostración de todas las funciones presentadas en este artículo:"

#, fuzzy
msgid "A little backstory on this release: it turns out, IBM had started to implement its own https://github.com/MicroShed/microprofile-language-server/[MicroProfile Language Server], providing MicroProfile support for https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-health[Health], Open API, Rest Client for `Java files` (validation, quick fixes, completions). In the meantime, the Red Hat's Quarkus Language Server had been refactored internally to split the Quarkus related bits from a MicroProfile focused core. Naturally, Red Hat and IBM realized there would be much value in contributing to a single MicroProfile Language Server implementation, and both parties agreed to join forces on developing the MicroProfile Language Server currently powering https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/[vscode-quarkus]."
msgstr "Un poco de historia sobre esta versión: resulta que IBM había comenzado a implementar su propio Servidor de Lenguaje  link:https://github.com/MicroShed/microprofile-language-server/[MicroProfile], proporcionando soporte MicroProfile para  link:https://github.com/eclipse/microprofile-health[Health], Open API, Rest Client para `Java files` (validación, correcciones rápidas, terminaciones). Mientras tanto, el Quarkus Language Server de Red Hat había sido refactorizado internamente para separar las partes relacionadas con Quarkus de un núcleo centrado en MicroProfile. Naturalmente, Red Hat e IBM se dieron cuenta de que sería muy valioso contribuir a la implementación de un único MicroProfile Language Server, y ambas partes acordaron unir fuerzas para desarrollar el MicroProfile Language Server que actualmente alimenta a  link:https://github.com/redhat-developer/vscode-quarkus/[vscode-quarkus]."

#, fuzzy
msgid "The outcome of this collaboration is the https://projects.eclipse.org/proposals/eclipse-lsp4mp-language-server-eclipse-microprofile-0[Eclipse LSP4MP (Language Server for Eclipse MicroProfile) project proposal]. So stay tuned for more announcements on that subject!"
msgstr "El resultado de esta colaboración es la  link:https://projects.eclipse.org/proposals/eclipse-lsp4mp-language-server-eclipse-microprofile-0[propuesta del proyecto Eclipse LSP4MP (Language Server for Eclipse MicroProfile)]. Así que permanezca atento a más anuncios al respecto."

